import InterviewQuestions from '../../components/tools/InterviewQuestions.jsx';
---
<BaseLayout title="Visa Interview Practice — Preparation Prompts" description="Use sample visa interview prompts to practise explaining your genuine travel purpose, course choice and funding accurately."><article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Visa Interview Question Practice</h1><p class="mb-8">These are practice prompts, not a verified transcript of embassy questions or a prediction of what you will be asked. Interview requirements vary by route.</p><InterviewQuestions client:load /><section class="prose max-w-none mt-10"><h2>Practise facts, not a script</h2><p>Explain the actual purpose, dates, funding and supporting circumstances in your own words. If a date or amount is uncertain, check it rather than inventing an answer. Read your submitted application before practising.</p><h2>Check that evidence and explanation agree</h2><p>For each prompt, identify which application detail it relates to. Check discrepancies in course names, employers, accommodation and payer details before an appointment. A confident delivery cannot replace the correct evidence.</p><h2>Use official appointment instructions</h2><p>Bring the documents requested for your own interview and follow security and language instructions. Do not assume that every embassy interviews every applicant or makes a decision in a fixed number of minutes.</p><h2>Know the limits</h2><p>These prompts do not score eligibility or guarantee approval. For case-specific legal questions, use a qualified adviser. Review the relevant <a href="/guides/">destination guide</a> and its official sources.</p></section></article></BaseLayout>
